data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2.0**, which targets **OpenAPI 3.1**. This is a major object-model rewrite. Here are the breaks in your code:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1.x) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2.x) | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | `JsonNode` (`JsonValue.Create(...)`) | `IOpenApiAny` hierarchy removed; uses `System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `schema.Example = ...` | `schema.Example = jsonNode` | Property type changed from `IOpenApiAny` → `JsonNode` |
| `schema.Nullable = bool` | Removed | OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's `type` array; add/remove `JsonSchemaType.Null` in `schema.Type` |
| `new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "..." }` + `OpenApiSecurityScheme` | `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("id")` | Typed reference classes replace generic `OpenApiReference` |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` keyed by `OpenApiSecurityScheme` | Keyed by `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference` | Follows from above |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;          // ← replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References; // ← new typed-reference classes

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString → JsonValue
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    // OpenApiResponse API is unchanged here
    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // OpenApiSecurityScheme + OpenApiReference → OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference
    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable property removed — strip the Null flag from the Type bitmask
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Key takeaways

1. **`Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone** — use `System.Text.Json.Nodes` (`JsonValue.Create(...)` for scalars, `JsonArray`/`JsonObject` for complex values).
2. **`Nullable` property removed** — `schema.Type` is now a `[Flags] enum JsonSchemaType`. Toggle nullability with `|= JsonSchemaType.Null` or `&= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`.
3. **Typed reference classes** in `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References` (`OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference`, `OpenApiSchemaReference`, etc.) replace the generic `OpenApiReference` + `ReferenceType` pattern.
